Our corrective framework is built on a rigorous axiomatic system that bridges operator theory and neural architecture design.

Definition 1 (Physical State-Space). Let \mathbb{X} be a compact, smooth manifold of physical states for the system under observation. A snapshot of the video defines a state x \in \mathbb{X}. The ground-truth evolution of this physical process is governed by a smooth flow \Phi^\tau such that x_\tau = \Phi^\tau(x_0).

Definition 2 (The Koopman Operator \mathcal{K}^\tau). This linear operator evolves any "observable function" g(x) of the system. Even for chaotic systems with highly nonlinear \Phi^\tau, the Koopman operator \mathcal{K}^\tau acts linearly on this function space. Our framework asserts that a truly robust AI should learn \mathcal{K}^\tau from video, as it encodes a complete and linear representation of the physics. This theoretical shift lies at the heart of earlier energy-based frameworks for cognition, where similar operators encode complete rules of dynamics .

Definition 3 (The Maakoul Cognitive Manifold \mathcal{M}_{\text{cog}}). We formally define the space of AI reasoning not as a flat Euclidean token-space, but as a Riemannian manifold (\mathcal{M}_{\text{cog}}, g) whose metric g is learned directly from data via diffusion maps. The practical advantage of this geometric constraint is that it directly improves cross-domain generalization, as it forces the model to represent its latent trajectory on the physically plausible, low-dimensional geometric structure of the system's dynamics. This concept is rooted in recent works showing that such manifold constraints are essential for accurate modeling of structured temporal data .

Definition 4 (The Perron-Frobenius (TF) Operator \mathcal{P}^\tau). The adjoint of the Koopman operator. It acts on probability distributions \rho(x) over the state space and governs how a cloud of uncertainty evolves over time. Our cognitive framework directly models the AI's "belief state" about a video as a probability density \rho_0. The crucial theoretical link is that reasoning about the physics of the video is itself the action of the TF operator: \rho_t = \mathcal{P}^t \rho_0.

· Axiom 1 (Conservation of Belief). For any valid reasoning chain, the total probability mass must be conserved: \int_{\mathcal{M}_{\text{cog}}} \rho_t(x) dx = 1, \forall t.
· Axiom 2 (Conservation of Energy/Momentum). For a valid reasoning chain, the physical invariants of the system I: \mathbb{X} \to \mathbb{R} must be conserved: \frac{d}{dt}I(x_t) = 0. We will enforce this at machine precision using architectural constraints.

